WEBVTT

00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:04.960
When a customer reads a card number aloud, the agent hears it and

00:00:04.960 --> 00:00:06.578
the recording keeps it.

00:00:06.578 --> 00:00:09.980
Secure data capture takes the agent out of that moment.

00:00:09.980 --> 00:00:14.107
This video shows the settings, how an agent sends the link, what the

00:00:14.107 --> 00:00:17.900
customer sees, what is kept, and what a production site needs.

00:00:22.500 --> 00:00:27.314
Card numbers read aloud end up in the agent's ears, in the recording,

00:00:27.314 --> 00:00:29.689
and sometimes on a sticky note.

00:00:29.689 --> 00:00:34.310
Pausing the recording helps, but the agent still hears the number.

00:00:35.060 --> 00:00:39.242
With secure capture, the agent sends the customer a one-time link.

00:00:39.242 --> 00:00:43.541
The customer types the number on their own device, on a secure page,

00:00:43.541 --> 00:00:47.200
and the platform tokenizes it the moment it is submitted.

00:00:47.950 --> 00:00:52.432
The agent, the supervisor and the recording never see the value.

00:00:52.432 --> 00:00:58.130
Only a masked reference is kept, and a security code is checked and then discarded.

00:01:02.429 --> 00:01:07.149
Open Settings, Contact Center, and choose the Secure Data Capture tab.

00:01:07.149 --> 00:01:10.999
It needs the Contact Center Secure Data Capture feature.

00:01:11.830 --> 00:01:15.034
Tick Enable agent-assisted secure data capture.

00:01:15.034 --> 00:01:19.508
While it is off, the platform refuses to start a capture, and agents

00:01:19.508 --> 00:01:21.140
never see the button.

00:01:21.815 --> 00:01:26.973
Capture link lifetime is how long the one-time link works before it expires.

00:01:26.973 --> 00:01:28.231
Keep it short.

00:01:28.231 --> 00:01:34.206
Pause recording during capture also pauses the recording for as long as the capture runs.

00:01:34.206 --> 00:01:35.275
Click Save.

00:01:39.538 --> 00:01:45.151
On a live call, the Active interaction panel in My workspace shows Collect data securely.

00:01:45.151 --> 00:01:49.227
It appears only when the setting is on and the agent's role has

00:01:49.227 --> 00:01:53.598
the permission to initiate secure capture, which the Agent role has.

00:01:54.110 --> 00:01:56.210
Click Collect data securely.

00:01:56.210 --> 00:02:00.471
The workspace shows a one-time link to share with the customer.

00:02:00.471 --> 00:02:06.090
Send it by text message, email or chat, whichever channel you already have with them.

00:02:06.582 --> 00:02:09.676
Only one capture can run on a call at a time.

00:02:09.676 --> 00:02:14.953
When the phone provider can pause recording, the recording stays paused while the

00:02:14.953 --> 00:02:18.349
customer types, and resumes when the capture ends.

00:02:18.349 --> 00:02:23.262
The provider of this demo site is unreachable, so nothing is recorded here.

00:02:27.562 --> 00:02:29.521
The customer opens the link.

00:02:29.521 --> 00:02:31.076
No sign-in is needed.

00:02:31.076 --> 00:02:35.051
The page says Secure page, and tells them that the agent on the

00:02:35.051 --> 00:02:37.182
call cannot see what they type.

00:02:37.732 --> 00:02:41.003
It asks for the details the capture requested:

00:02:41.003 --> 00:02:44.148
Card number, Card expiry, and Security code.

00:02:44.148 --> 00:02:48.362
Here we type the standard test card number, never a real one.

00:02:48.857 --> 00:02:51.710
The customer clicks Submit securely.

00:02:51.710 --> 00:02:57.076
An invalid card number is refused on the page, and the link stays usable.

00:02:57.076 --> 00:02:59.997
A valid one ends on a Thank you page.

00:03:04.197 --> 00:03:07.934
The customer sees Thank you, and recording resumes.

00:03:07.934 --> 00:03:13.967
If the customer never finishes, the link expires and the recording resumes on its own.

00:03:14.717 --> 00:03:18.934
What the platform keeps is a masked reference, such as the last four

00:03:18.934 --> 00:03:20.245
digits of a card.

00:03:20.245 --> 00:03:22.696
The security code is not kept at all.

00:03:22.696 --> 00:03:26.856
The agent's screen does not show the value, and no admin list shows

00:03:26.856 --> 00:03:28.737
the masked reference today.

00:03:29.487 --> 00:03:34.890
Starting, completing and cancelling a capture are recorded as events, so a workflow

00:03:34.890 --> 00:03:36.347
can react to them.

00:03:40.647 --> 00:03:45.554
The tokenizing used in this video is for development and evaluation only.

00:03:45.554 --> 00:03:53.007
Outside the Development environment, no tokenization is available until a developer connects a compliant provider.

00:03:53.457 --> 00:03:56.616
Until then, the secure capture fails closed.

00:03:56.616 --> 00:04:01.292
The agent can still send a link, but when the customer submits valid

00:04:01.292 --> 00:04:05.083
details, the page refuses them and shows this message.

00:04:05.083 --> 00:04:07.357
No sensitive data is accepted.

00:04:11.557 --> 00:04:15.902
A billing agent takes a card payment over the phone, and the customer

00:04:15.902 --> 00:04:18.277
enters the card on the secure page.

00:04:19.027 --> 00:04:24.567
A support agent collects a bank account number to set up a refund, without hearing it.

00:04:25.317 --> 00:04:31.867
A company adds a national identification number to an identity check, with the same one-time link.

00:04:32.617 --> 00:04:38.307
A supervisor reviewing a recording never hears a card number, because the customer typed it.

00:04:40.307 --> 00:04:44.691
Turn on the setting, send the link, let the customer type, and connect

00:04:44.691 --> 00:04:47.517
a tokenization provider before you go live.

00:04:47.517 --> 00:04:49.017
Thanks for watching.

